&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the Product Development Team as a BMS Application Engineer focused on delivering high-voltage battery systems for electric vehicles. This is an exciting opportunity to be part of a fast-growing team in the battery industry and contribute to the next generation of EV technology within a Tier 1 supplier environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the design and development of the electrical architecture of high-voltage battery systems, including BMS, CMU.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting in translating customer and system-level requirements into feasible design and software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with cross-functional teams (BMS HW, BMS SW, FuSa, Systems, Testing) to ensure complete system integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participating in RFQ/RFI processes by preparing technical input and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting BMS hardware integration and communication interfaces (CAN/LIN).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to system validation, including electrical testing and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting DFMEA, DVP&amp;amp;R planning, and functional safety efforts aligned with ISO 26262.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onsite OEM support for flashing, initial integration, troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with global teams, including some travel to suppliers or OEM sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications (Required):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, Mechanical or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of relevant experience in the battery or EV industry, preferably in a BMS hardware or software role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to high-voltage battery systems (400–1000V) including electronic/sw design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of BMS, CAN communication, and automotive diagnostic protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of APQP, PPAP, and automotive product development cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of safety standards such as ISO 26262.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and collaborative mindset with strong communication skills in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual Chinese is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 15%, including visits to suppliers and OEMs, both domestic and international.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
