&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gotion Inc. is based in Silicon Valley, CA, currently building a Manufacturing facility in Manteno, IL and has R&amp;amp;D centers in Ohio, China, Japan and Europe. We innovate in the next generation electric vehicle and energy storage technologies (lithium batteries and related systems) with the aim to accelerate electrified transportation and achieve sustainable development. Gotion is powered by a leading power battery technology company that provides solutions for vehicles including the world&#39;s first mass commercial e-bus route.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Gotion is a career destination - we are not simply attempting to just fill another job, but to pursue a dream of global green energy together! We offer outstanding opportunities to individuals seeking an exciting and challenging working environment. Everyone is highly valued and plays a vital role in the growth of our organization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Construction Cost Estimator / Cost Engineer (Mandarin Required)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Manteno, Illinois&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Type:&lt;/strong&gt; Full-Time&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;$75,000 – $90,000 annually&lt;/strong&gt; (based on experience)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gotion is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Mandarin-speaking Construction Cost Estimator / Cost Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to support the planning, estimating, budgeting, and cost control of large-scale industrial construction projects at our Manteno, Illinois facility. This role serves as a key liaison between U.S. contractors, design teams, suppliers, and Gotion&#39;s Chinese management and engineering teams. The successful candidate will be responsible for preparing accurate cost estimates, evaluating contractor proposals, managing project budgets, and providing cost analysis throughout all phases of construction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has experience with industrial or commercial construction estimating, strong analytical skills, and is &lt;strong&gt;fluent in both English and Mandarin Chinese&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare quantity takeoffs, conceptual estimates, detailed cost estimates, and project budgets for industrial buildings, civil, architectural, MEP, and site development projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review construction drawings, technical specifications, bid documents, and contracts to ensure accurate pricing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze contractor and supplier proposals, identifying scope gaps, duplicated costs, pricing discrepancies, and value engineering opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare bid control estimates, cost analyses, budget forecasts, and financial reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review pricing for Potential Change Orders (PCOs), Change Orders (COs), and other contract modifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify contractor labor, material, equipment, subcontractor, overhead, and profit costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in procurement activities, bid evaluations, commercial negotiations, and contract pricing reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
