&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gotion Inc. is based in Silicon Valley, CA, currently building a Manufacturing facility in Manteno, IL and has R&amp;amp;D centers in Ohio, China, Japan and Europe. We innovate in the next generation electric vehicle and energy storage technologies (lithium batteries and related systems) with the aim to accelerate electrified transportation and achieve sustainable development. Gotion is powered by a leading power battery technology company that provides solutions for vehicles including the world&#39;s first mass commercial e-bus route.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Gotion is a career destination - we are not simply attempting to just fill another job, but to pursue a dream of global green energy together! We offer outstanding opportunities to individuals seeking an exciting and challenging working environment. Everyone is highly valued and plays a vital role in the growth of our organization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Electrical Engineer – Construction &amp;amp; Capital Projects&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Manteno, IL&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt; Engineering / Capital Projects&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Arrangement:&lt;/strong&gt; 100% On-Site&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated &lt;strong&gt;Electrical Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to support the planning, design, construction, and commissioning of electrical infrastructure for large-scale industrial and manufacturing facilities. This role will provide technical expertise for facility expansion, utility infrastructure, and capital construction projects while collaborating with engineering, construction, operations, and maintenance teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has experience designing and supporting industrial electrical systems, is proficient in AutoCAD and/or SolidWorks, and possesses strong knowledge of medium-voltage and low-voltage power distribution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and support electrical systems for new construction, facility expansions, and capital improvement projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, review, and revise electrical drawings, one-line diagrams, panel schedules, wiring diagrams, and installation packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and modify engineering drawings using &lt;strong&gt;AutoCAD and/or SolidWorks&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support construction teams throughout project execution, ensuring installations meet engineering specifications and applicable codes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with mechanical, civil, controls, facilities, and construction teams to ensure seamless project execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with equipment selection, electrical load calculations, short-circuit studies, voltage drop calculations, and system sizing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical support during equipment installation, startup, commissioning, and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review contractor submittals, RFIs, engineering change requests, and as-built documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support electrical infrastructure improvements for manufacturing equipment and facility utilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with NEC, NFPA, OSHA, and applicable local electrical codes and standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in project planning, scheduling, budgeting, and execution of multiple capital projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in Electrical Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3–5 years&lt;/strong&gt; of experience supporting industrial, manufacturing, or construction projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in manufacturing facilities, industrial plants, or large commercial construction environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of engineering documentation and construction practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Technical Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Electrical Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert knowledge of &lt;strong&gt;facility electrical distribution systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;external utility electrical infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of &lt;strong&gt;medium-voltage electrical systems and below&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of low-voltage power distribution systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical equipment sizing and specification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Power distribution design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical load calculations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voltage drop calculations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short-circuit and coordination principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Software&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in &lt;strong&gt;AutoCAD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;SolidWorks&lt;/strong&gt; preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to create and modify engineering drawings and electrical layouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Documentation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read, interpret, create, and revise:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical one-line diagrams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Three-line diagrams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wiring diagrams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Panel schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Control schematics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Construction drawings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equipment layouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As-built documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated with the ability to manage multiple priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time management abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively with cross-functional engineering and construction teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented with a commitment to quality and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting industrial construction or capital projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of industrial power distribution, substations, switchgear, transformers, MCCs, and backup power systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with utility coordination and electrical permitting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with contractors during construction and commissioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of PLC-controlled manufacturing environments is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer-in-Training (EIT) certification or Professional Engineer (PE) license is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produces accurate, high-quality electrical designs and engineering documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports successful execution of construction projects from design through commissioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborates effectively with engineering, facilities, operations, and construction teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivers technically sound solutions that improve reliability, safety, and maintainability of facility electrical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures projects are completed on schedule while meeting quality, safety, and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
