&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title:&lt;/strong&gt; HR Business Partner / Employee Relations Specialist&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Manteno, IL&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Schedule:&lt;/strong&gt; Fully On-site, Monday–Friday&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Type:&lt;/strong&gt; Full-time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience Level:&lt;/strong&gt; 5–10 years&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language Requirement:&lt;/strong&gt; English and Spanish bilingual required&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gotion is seeking a hands-on HR Business Partner / Employee Relations Specialist to support our business and R&amp;amp;D teams in Manteno, Illinois. This role is designed for an execution-oriented HR professional who can work closely with managers and employees on employee relations, 90-day reviews, performance management, documentation, corrective actions, investigations, and day-to-day HR support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a fully on-site role, Monday through Friday. The ideal candidate should be comfortable working directly with business leaders, technical managers, R&amp;amp;D teams, and employees in a fast-paced, cross-functional environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead and support employee relations matters, including employee complaints, workplace concerns, misconduct issues, communication conflicts, attendance concerns, policy violations, and manager-employee disputes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conduct workplace investigations, document findings, summarize facts, and recommend appropriate next steps in partnership with HR leadership and management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support the 90-day review process for new hires, including review tracking, manager follow-up, documentation, performance feedback, and employment decision support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with business and R&amp;amp;D managers on performance management, including coaching conversations, performance documentation, corrective action, PIP support, and follow-up actions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maintain strong on-site visibility and build effective working relationships with employees, managers, and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide Spanish-language HR support when needed, including policy explanation, employee communication, investigation interviews, coaching, and issue resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ensure consistent application of company policies, performance standards, attendance expectations, disciplinary processes, and workplace conduct requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prepare and maintain accurate HR documentation, including investigation notes, corrective action forms, 90-day review records, performance documentation, and employee relations case files.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coach managers on handling difficult employee conversations in a compliant, practical, and well-documented manner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with HR leadership, legal, payroll, operations, and functional leaders on employee relations, performance, compliance, leave, attendance, and workforce management issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify recurring ER or performance issues and recommend practical improvements to reduce risk, improve accountability, and strengthen team effectiveness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support additional HR activities as needed, including onboarding, employee communication, HR reporting, policy rollout, employee engagement, and manager enablement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5–10 years of HR experience, with strong hands-on experience in employee relations, performance management, corrective actions, workplace investigations, and manager coaching.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior experience supporting business, technical, R&amp;amp;D, engineering, commercial, project, or cross-functional teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fluent or professional working proficiency in both English and Spanish.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong understanding of employee relations documentation, investigation processes, corrective action, attendance management, and performance review processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to work fully on-site in Manteno, IL, Monday through Friday.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfortable working directly with managers, employees, technical teams, and business leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong judgment, confidentiality, documentation discipline, and ability to handle sensitive employee matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to operate in a fast-paced environment where HR must be visible, responsive, practical, and execution-focused.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong communication skills, including the ability to explain policies, expectations, and performance feedback clearly in both English and Spanish.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience supporting 90-day reviews, probationary period evaluations, structured new-hire performance reviews, or manager-led performance calibration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience supporting R&amp;amp;D, engineering, product, commercial, sales, project management, or technical business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in battery, EV, clean energy, automotive, technology, advanced manufacturing, or high-growth industrial environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of Illinois employment practices and general U.S. employment law principles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with HRIS, case tracking, attendance systems, performance documentation systems, or employee relations case management tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideal Candidate Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a practical, on-site HR operator who can support business and R&amp;amp;D teams with discipline, speed, and sound judgment. This person should be able to handle employee relations cases independently, follow through on 90-day reviews and performance actions, coach managers through difficult conversations, and keep documentation clean and defensible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is best suited for someone who is not looking for a purely strategic HR role. We need someone who can execute, follow up, document, communicate clearly, and help managers build accountability across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation will be based on experience, qualifications, and internal equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manteno, IL&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fully on-site, Monday–Friday&lt;/p&gt;
