&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inventory Control Specialist&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Inventory Control Specialist is responsible for maintaining accurate inventory records, ensuring inventory integrity, and supporting warehouse and production operations through effective inventory management practices. This position works closely with Warehouse, Production, Logistics, Purchasing, Quality, and Finance teams to ensure timely and accurate inventory transactions, reconciliation, reporting, and compliance with company procedures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inventory Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and maintain inventory accuracy within ERP/WMS systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process inventory transactions including receipts, transfers, adjustments, returns, and shipments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform daily inventory reconciliation and investigate inventory discrepancies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct cycle counts and support physical inventory activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze inventory variances and identify root causes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend corrective actions to prevent recurring inventory issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ERP/WMS Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all inventory transactions are accurately recorded in ERP and Warehouse Management Systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and validate inventory data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support system troubleshooting and resolve inventory-related transaction errors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with ERP/WMS process improvements and optimization initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Production teams to ensure material availability and inventory accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Logistics and Warehouse teams regarding material movement and inventory transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Purchasing and Supply Chain teams to resolve receiving and inventory discrepancies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Finance during inventory reconciliation and month-end closing activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting and Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare daily, weekly, and monthly inventory reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track inventory KPIs including inventory accuracy, inventory aging, cycle count performance, and material shortages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze inventory trends and provide recommendations for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support management with inventory performance metrics and operational reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance and Audit Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with company inventory control policies and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain documentation supporting inventory transactions and adjustments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with internal and external audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support implementation of inventory control best practices and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve inventory accuracy and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in warehouse and supply chain improvement projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Lean Manufacturing and continuous improvement activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate’s Degree or Bachelor’s Degree in Supply Chain Management, Logistics, Business Administration, Operations Management, or a related field preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3 years of inventory control, warehouse operations, logistics, or supply chain experience in a manufacturing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP systems (SAP preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Warehouse Management Systems (WMS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Battery manufacturing, automotive, or high-volume manufacturing experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of inventory control principles and warehouse operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with ERP and WMS systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Microsoft Excel skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to investigate and resolve inventory discrepancies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and cross-functional coordination skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented with a high degree of accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a warehouse and manufacturing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stand, walk, and move throughout the facility for extended periods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to occasionally lift up to 25 pounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to perform cycle counts and physical inventory verification activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Conditions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manufacturing and warehouse environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;May require occasional overtime, weekend work, or support during physical inventory activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reports To: Warehouse Manager&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;xmsonormal&quot;&gt;Base pay is one part of our total compensation package at Gotion, and is determined within a range. This provides you with the opportunity to progress as you grow and advance your career at Gotion. The base pay range for this role is shown below, and will depend on your skills, qualifications, experiences, and location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Expected Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$24&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$26 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Gotion Inc. is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We are dedicated to fostering a diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve, cultivating a culture of inclusion and belonging, and ensuring equal employment opportunities for all.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We provide equal opportunity to all individuals regardless of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related conditions (including breastfeeding), parental status, criminal histories consistent with legal requirements, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Gotion Inc., we strive to create an environment where everyone feels valued, respected, and empowered to thrive.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gotion Inc. is based in Silicon Valley, CA, currently building a Manufacturing facility in Manteno, IL and has R&amp;amp;D centers in Ohio, China, Japan and Europe. We innovate in the next generation electric vehicle and energy storage technologies (lithium batteries and related systems) with the aim to accelerate electrified transportation and achieve sustainable development. Gotion is powered by a leading power battery technology company that provides solutions for vehicles including the world&#39;s first mass commercial e-bus route.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Gotion is a career destination - we are not simply attempting to just fill another job, but to pursue a dream of global green energy together! We offer outstanding opportunities to individuals seeking an exciting and challenging working environment. Everyone is highly valued and plays a vital role in the growth of our organization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About Gotion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Gotion, Inc. is a leading manufacturer of advanced battery technologies, committed to driving the clean energy transition. As we scale operations in Illinois, we seek talented individuals to join our dynamic and innovative team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Position Overview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are seeking an experienced and bilingual IT Manager to lead our IT network infrastructure initiatives in Manteno, IL. This individual will play a critical role in designing, implementing, and maintaining a secure and efficient IT network, ensuring seamless operations across our facilities. Fluency in both English and at least business level Chinese is required to support communication with global teams and vendors.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
