&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gotion Inc. is based in Silicon Valley, CA, currently building a Manufacturing facility in Manteno, IL and has R&amp;amp;D centers in Ohio, China, Japan and Europe. We innovate in the next generation electric vehicle and energy storage technologies (lithium batteries and related systems) with the aim to accelerate electrified transportation and achieve sustainable development. Gotion is powered by a leading power battery technology company that provides solutions for vehicles including the world&#39;s first mass commercial e-bus route.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Gotion is a career destination - we are not simply attempting to just fill another job, but to pursue a dream of global green energy together! We offer outstanding opportunities to individuals seeking an exciting and challenging working environment. Everyone is highly valued and plays a vital role in the growth of our organization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gotion is seeking a motivated and results-driven &lt;strong&gt;Process Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to support the Pack and Module Manufacturing team. This role is responsible for developing, optimizing, and sustaining manufacturing processes to ensure safe, efficient, and high-quality production. The Process Engineer will play a key role in supporting production ramp-up activities, driving continuous improvement initiatives, resolving manufacturing issues, and implementing process enhancements to improve yield, throughput, and overall equipment effectiveness (OEE).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have experience in manufacturing engineering, strong problem-solving skills, and a passion for improving production processes in a fast-paced manufacturing environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure stable manufacturing processes within the Pack and Module production lines, achieving target yield, process capability, throughput, and OEE goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the selection, evaluation, and implementation of manufacturing processes, equipment, and technical requirements for new and existing production lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering support activities during equipment installation, commissioning, validation, trial runs, and production ramp-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Quality, Production, Maintenance, and other cross-functional teams to establish and maintain effective control plans and in-process quality controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot process-related issues on the production floor and drive timely corrective and preventive actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize structured problem-solving methodologies and quality tools to identify root causes and prevent issue recurrence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, review, and maintain process documentation including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process Flow Diagrams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work Instructions (WIs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process Standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Control Plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute process experiments, collect and analyze process data, and provide recommendations for process optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support continuous improvement initiatives focused on safety, quality, productivity, yield, and cost reduction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in equipment and process qualifications for new products, equipment, and manufacturing technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze manufacturing performance metrics and identify opportunities to improve product quality and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct training and provide technical guidance to production personnel on manufacturing processes and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support new product introductions and manufacturing readiness activities.&lt;/li&gt;
