&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production &amp;amp; Shop-floor Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement production plans to meet deadlines and production targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and manage production progress, quality metrics, and costs to improve overall efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain 5S standards and Visual Management systems to ensure a clean, organized, and transparent work environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct daily Gemba walks to identify and resolve floor-level bottlenecks in real-time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize workflows through lean manufacturing practices and reduce production waste.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equipment and Process Oversight:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the maintenance and operation of production equipment to ensure consistent performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement initiatives and implement smart manufacturing techniques where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, train, and manage a high-performing production team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate team performance regularly and foster a collaborative work environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage labor relations and conflict resolution effectively within a diverse workforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration and Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with R&amp;amp;D, Quality, and Procurement teams to support new product launches and stabilize production processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with ISO9001, ISO14001, and other quality management standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety and Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce safety regulations to maintain a safe working environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare detailed production reports, analyze data, and provide actionable insights to management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or above in Industrial Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Automation, or related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 5 years of experience in manufacturing production management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3 years in a managerial role, preferably in large-scale production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with lean manufacturing, Six Sigma, or similar methodologies is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive understanding of manufacturing processes, production techniques, and equipment management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong capabilities in production planning, cost control, quality assurance, and efficiency improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ERP systems and production management software (e.g., SAP, MES)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional leadership, communication, and team management abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset with the ability to make data-driven decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of responsibility and resilience in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilience and the ability to lead a team through high-pressure production ramps and process stabilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The U.S. base salary range for this full-time position is $100,000.00 - $150,000.00, plus eligibility for bonus and benefits. Our salary ranges are determined by factors such as the role, level, and geographic location. The range listed in the job posting represents the minimum and maximum target salaries for this position across all U.S. locations. Actual compensation within the range will be influenced by the specific work location, along with factors such as job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter will provide more details about the specific salary range for your preferred location during the hiring process. Please note that the listed compensation reflects the base salary only and does not include bonus or benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Gotion Inc. is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We are dedicated to fostering a diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve, cultivating a culture of inclusion and belonging, and ensuring equal employment opportunities for all.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We provide equal opportunity to all individuals regardless of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related conditions (including breastfeeding), parental status, criminal histories consistent with legal requirements, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
