&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gotion Inc. is based in Silicon Valley, CA, currently building a Manufacturing facility in Manteno, IL and has R&amp;amp;D centers in Ohio, China, Japan and Europe. We innovate in the next generation electric vehicle and energy storage technologies (lithium batteries and related systems) with the aim to accelerate electrified transportation and achieve sustainable development. Gotion is powered by a leading power battery technology company that provides solutions for vehicles including the world&#39;s first mass commercial e-bus route.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Gotion is a career destination - we are not simply attempting to just fill another job, but to pursue a dream of global green energy together! We offer outstanding opportunities to individuals seeking an exciting and challenging working environment. Everyone is highly valued and plays a vital role in the growth of our organization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role &amp;amp; Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the Product Development Team as a Senior Electrical Engineer focused on delivering high-voltage battery systems for electric vehicles. This is an exciting opportunity to be part of a fast-growing team in the battery industry and contribute to the next generation of EV technology within a Tier 1 supplier environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the design and development of the electrical architecture of high-voltage battery systems, including BDU components such as contactors, fuses, FPC, CCS, sensors, busbar and wiring.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting in translating customer and system-level requirements into feasible and manufacturable design solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with cross-functional teams (mechanical, thermal, software, testing) to ensure complete system integration.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participating in RFQ/RFI processes by preparing technical input and documentation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting BMS hardware integration and communication interfaces (CAN/LIN).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to system validation, including electrical testing and troubleshooting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting DFMEA, DVP&amp;amp;R planning, and functional safety efforts aligned with ISO 26262.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engaging with suppliers to review and qualify electrical components.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with global teams, including limited travel to suppliers or OEM sites.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, Mechanical or a related field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of relevant experience in the battery or EV industry, preferably in a Design and development or validation role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to high-voltage battery systems (400–1000V) including pack or module-level design.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of BMS, CAN communication, and automotive diagnostic protocols.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CAD tools such as Catia V6 – Electrical and Capital Harness/Busbar.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
