&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gotion Inc. is based in Silicon Valley, CA, currently building a Manufacturing facility in Manteno, IL and has R&amp;amp;D centers in Ohio, China, Japan and Europe. We innovate in the next generation electric vehicle and energy storage technologies (lithium batteries and related systems) with the aim to accelerate electrified transportation and achieve sustainable development. Gotion is powered by a leading power battery technology company that provides solutions for vehicles including the world&#39;s first mass commercial e-bus route.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Gotion is a career destination - we are not simply attempting to just fill another job, but to pursue a dream of global green energy together! We offer outstanding opportunities to individuals seeking an exciting and challenging working environment. Everyone is highly valued and plays a vital role in the growth of our organization.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gotion is seeking a Technical Program Manager to spearhead US OEM customer projects in cell product development. In this role, you will lead the initiatives from concept through to production, coordinating closely with both our customers and our headquarter cell team. This position is ideal for someone with a robust engineering background and a masterful grasp of project management in the battery cell technology sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Directly engage with US OEM customers, driving and coordinating cell development and manufacturing in tandem with the headquarter cell team.&lt;br&gt;Manage projects from conception to production handover, acting as the main point of contact throughout the process.&lt;br&gt;Develop detailed manufacturing program plans, defining strategy, scope, schedule, resources, and cost targets.&lt;br&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to align the manufacturing program with the planned objectives.&lt;br&gt;Create, maintain, and effectively communicate project schedules to engineering leadership.&lt;br&gt;Identify innovative solutions to overcome project obstacles and maintain schedule adherence.&lt;br&gt;Prioritize and track the progress of cross-functional team tasks, balancing schedule, risk, resources, and outcomes.&lt;br&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Master’s Degree or higher in Materials Science, Chemical Engineering, or a related field.&lt;br&gt;Extensive knowledge and strong industry experience in lithium-ion battery cell technology.&lt;br&gt;Minimum of 5 years in product development or manufacturing, with a mix of engineering and project management roles.&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage engineering projects for mass-produced products.&lt;br&gt;Proficiency in project management tools like JIRA, Microsoft Project, and Confluence.&lt;br&gt;Ability to work effectively across functions and manage large teams.&lt;br&gt;Willingness to travel as required for project needs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;xmsonormal&quot;&gt;Base pay is one part of our total compensation package at Gotion, and is determined within a range. This provides you with the opportunity to progress as you grow and advance your career at Gotion. The base pay range for this role is shown below, and will depend on your skills, qualifications, experiences, and location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Expected Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$100,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Gotion Inc. is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We are dedicated to fostering a diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve, cultivating a culture of inclusion and belonging, and ensuring equal employment opportunities for all.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
